                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Qualify the brief before you design anything`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `Helvetia signed: 600 managers, five regions, one transformation journey that must feel local everywhere — for a fixed <strong>$4.5M</strong> (about $7,500 a head). The instinct is to say yes to everything, but that is exactly the flagship that delivered <em>NPS 74 at a 9% margin</em> last year. Before designing, <strong>qualify the brief</strong>: separate what is genuinely Helvetia-specific (its transformation strategy, its competency model) from generic leadership content you already own, and tell real regional difference — language, regulation, market cases — from the “tailoring theatre” regional HR asks for out of habit. Then test whether the brief is fundable at the dean's <strong>25% floor</strong>.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Decide the off-the-shelf vs configured vs bespoke mix`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `The central design decision. Classify every module as <strong>off-the-shelf</strong> (existing content, cheap, reusable), <strong>configured</strong> (off-the-shelf rebuilt around Helvetia's own cases and data — the high-leverage middle), or <strong>fully bespoke</strong> (built from scratch, ~$90k and faculty-intensive). The art is a strong common <strong>core platform</strong> plus a thin, high-impact configured layer per region. Concentrate bespoke spend on the one or two modules that carry Helvetia's transformation strategy — and resist the trap of treating design as off-the-shelf vs bespoke only, forgoing the configured middle where most of the perceived value lives.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Stage the multi-region rollout under capacity & margin`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Constraints bite hardest here. Sequence the five regional launches across 12 months and allocate the <strong>70 faculty-days</strong> so no marquee professor exceeds safe utilisation. The marquee bench is already <em>above 80%</em>, and two have warned they will step back — over-book them to please Helvetia and you win this engagement but lose the faculty you need for the other 54. Extend the bench with <strong>regional faculty</strong> (~$9.5k/day vs ~$24k marquee) and <strong>train-the-facilitator</strong> cohorts, choose <strong>pilot-then-scale</strong> over a risky parallel launch, and price configured-module reuse into the margin bridge so every region clears 25%.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Lock the scorecard & pitch the global academy`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Set the engagement scorecard across all four KPIs — <strong>NPS, gross margin, faculty utilisation, on-time delivery</strong> — and pitch Year 1 of the <strong>$13M three-year academy</strong> to Helvetia's CHRO. The CHRO probes for the two failure modes: a <em>money-losing crowd-pleaser</em> (max NPS, margin gone, faculty at 95%) and a <em>margin-safe generic programme</em> that erodes NPS. Maximising any single KPI degrades the others. The CHRO will also dangle $1M more to make every region fully bespoke — would your bench survive it, and would the dean sign?`,

